<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  PyrelandsWeather_RuledTable.xml   RimUtinni: Fire Ecology   2026-09-11
  ============================================================================
  PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1's last owed line: "the ruled weather table"
  (the_pyrelands.md, "Owed"). Stage0 and BlackRain, in this same folder,
  already did the two things FIRE_ECOLOGY_LOOP_1 budgeted — strip the rain,
  crank the dry thunderstorm, wire Black Rain in at a low base. What they did
  NOT do is finish the table, and the sheet's own register (§9: "a horizon
  that is always smoking somewhere"; §3: ash "falling out of the sky for days
  after a big burn") is still missing from the campaign's biome.

  🔑 THE TARGET IS NOT INVENTED. mandrake.rm.pyrelands ships its own ruled
  table on its own biome — RM_FE_Pyrelands, in
  src/RimMandrake/Pyrelands/Defs/BiomeDefs/Pyrelands.xml — authored from the
  same canon:

      Clear 40 · DryThunderstorm 20 · AshFall 14 · Cinderfall 4 ·
      BlackRain 3 · Fog 2 · GrayPall 1 · Windy 2 · Overcast 2

  This file brings ZBiome_Grasslands (the campaign's Pyrelands) into line with
  that, scaled to the commonalities Stage0 already set here. Stage0 left
  Clear at 55 against the RM table's 40, a factor of ~1.375, so:

      AshFall    14 * 1.375  ->  19
      Cinderfall  4 * 1.375  ->   6

  ⛔ BLACK RAIN IS DELIBERATELY NOT RAISED to the RM table's 3. Its own file
  (PyrelandsWeather_BlackRain.xml) explains at length why 1 is correct HERE:
  WeatherDecider's ChanceFactorRainOnFire multiplies it 15x exactly while a
  large fire is burning, and Stage0 left it the only rain-rated weather in the
  table, so 1 already means "almost never, except when the map is alight".
  That is a reasoned, cited number and this file does not second-guess it.

  ⛔ WINDY AND OVERCAST are likewise left at Stage0's 0.5 rather than raised to
  the RM table's 2: neither is a Pyrelands signature, both are Odyssey-gated on
  the donor def, and the sheet rules nothing about them.

  SNOW IS REMOVED, and the RM biome's own comment is the reason: "this biome's
  placement band starts at 25 degC, so SnowGentle/SnowHard could never fire
  anyway (their temperatureRange is -999~-0.5)". The Pyrelands' measured temp
  median is 53.6 degC (§0). Two dead entries in a weighted table are noise that
  reads as a mistake to the next person who opens it.
  ⚠️ Both removes are wrapped in PatchOperationConditional rather than run bare:
  Stage0's header recorded SnowGentle 4 / SnowHard 4 in the live table on
  2026-09-01, but a donor update could drop them, and a PatchOperationRemove
  that matches nothing logs red. The conditional makes a changed donor a
  silent no-op instead.

  ORDER-INDEPENDENT. Patch files inside one mod's Patches/ folder apply
  alphabetically, so this one runs BEFORE Stage0 ("R" < "S"). That is fine:
  every operation here touches keys Stage0 and BlackRain never mention
  (AshFall, Cinderfall, SnowGentle, SnowHard), so there is no ordering
  dependency in either direction.

  ⚠️ This only changes what a Pyrelands map's weather decider rolls FROM.
  Existing saves pick it up on the next weather roll; no map regeneration is
  needed, unlike the terrain patch in this same folder.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>More Vanilla Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- The two weathers that make the horizon smoke. Both ship in
             mandrake.rm.pyrelands, which is a hard modDependency of this mod,
             so neither needs a MayRequire. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities</xpath>
          <value>
            <RM_FE_Weather_AshFall>19</RM_FE_Weather_AshFall>
            <RM_FE_Weather_Cinderfall>6</RM_FE_Weather_Cinderfall>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Snow, if the donor still has it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities/SnowGentle</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities/SnowGentle</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities/SnowHard</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities/SnowHard</xpath>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
